  "quality_scope": "23 real-model archive scenarios on each runtime include four fresh held-out questions authored after the final template freeze. Earlier exposed held-out examples are regression cases. The 22 prior History fixtures are regressions, not fresh held-out evidence. Comparisons remain provisional and model interpretations/source statements are not certified facts.",
  "development_notes": [
    "The prototype initially cached the retrieval child under the wrong parent field; fixed the search projection before qualification.",
    "Development negation/context cases exposed conservative interpretation disagreements. The version-2 shared choice template retains original general instructions and adds explicit negative/contextual-paraphrase guidance. Confidence and request byte defaults remain unchanged. Longer/compressed intermediate templates were rejected by request-size/joint-evidence regressions. The final template passes all22 prior History fixtures plus the fresh archive cohort.",
    "The first generated-suite admission rejected inherited recipe metadata. Rebound only the disposable canonical test manifest from the official failed-attempt recipe, obtained a fresh reviewed input plan and passed complete formal acceptance. CLI owns committed cache and receipt material.",
    "Harness corrections distinguish stage call and time budgets for uncertain-request recovery, default configuration revision, and explicit correction provenance/question scope. Current-vs-recorded template migration is independently exercised with the actual prior binary on native and Docker.",
    "Bootstrap fixture suites serialize their documented default-port check when independently scheduled in parallel. This does not change application behavior."
  ],
  "superseded_test_failures": [
    {
      "suite": "native history lifecycle capacity fixture",
      "reason": "Its1800-byte question hit the existing6144-byte request bound before reaching its intended state cap with the revised template. Set only this fixture request bound to8192; retain the1MiB state cap, separate request-limit checks and exact RESOURCE_LIMIT/hot-recovery assertions. The complete14-group rerun passes on the same artifact.",
      "passing_report": "verification/archive-history-lifecycle.json"
    },
    {
      "suite": "container documented-runner readiness fixture",
      "reason": "The implicit100-attempt polling loop expired before cold compilation completed. Independent documented-runner startup measured 19.168 seconds with zero restarts/OOM. Use an explicit45-second readiness deadline consistent with the other runtime harness; retain every deployment, health, hot-config, backup/restore and credential assertion. The complete34-case rerun must pass on the identical image.",
      "passing_report": "verification/archive-container-sdk.json",
      "observed_cold_start_seconds": 19.167948784001055
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Natural-language intent is fallible; callers requiring completeness set complete:true.",
    "Bounded candidate answers never prove exhaustive evidence. Full scans may remain partial on original/context/request/aggregation limits.",
    "Audit probability is exact under the declared uniform256 model; successful-search eligibility, incomplete audits and budget resumptions remain distinct populations/trials.",
    "Operator model versions are assertions, not provider-weight attestations.",
    "Feedback/replay and adaptive index promotion retain independent SEARCH-003 and INDEX-001 gates. Upstream issue97 tracks ordinary accepted-source export."
